diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..f6ff5b3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,38 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+Sign-in and registration offer passkeys and a password alternative. Account settings
+at `/devtools-times/account/settings` allow readers to add, rename, and remove
+passkeys, confirm their identity, and sign out. Removing the last passkey on a
+passwordless account is blocked to prevent lockout. Sensitive changes require an
+identity confirmation within the last five minutes.
+
+The WebAuthn implementation uses SimpleWebAuthn with discoverable credentials,
+required user verification, single-use five-minute challenges, and origin/RP
+verification. Authentication sessions use opaque, HTTP-only, SameSite cookies.
+New accounts, public credentials, password hashes, and sessions are stored in
+SQLite; biometric data and private keys are never sent to the app. Existing
+password-service users can sign in with their original credentials; a successful
+login provisions their local account for passkey enrollment. New accounts are
+managed by the local account service.
+
+Use Node.js 24 or later (the account store uses `node:sqlite`). Set these environment
+variables when deploying:
+
+- `AUTH_ORIGIN`: the exact public origin, such as `https://news.example.com`,
+  without a path or trailing slash. This must match the browser origin and be
+  configured when running behind a reverse proxy. It defaults to the request
+  origin for local use.
+- `AUTH_DB_PATH`: a persistent SQLite file, defaulting to `./data/auth.sqlite`.
+  Mount persistent storage and back it up. This store is intended for a single
+  application instance; a deployment with multiple replicas needs shared account
+  and session storage before enabling accounts.
+
+Passkeys require HTTPS, except on localhost. Browser support and cancellation
+failures are explained in the UI, with password fallback where available.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for account-store security checks, and `pnpm build` for the
+production build. No server is needed for these checks.
